    "notes": [
      "The stated idea says the town's name sits over the photograph, but the headline occupies rows 2–3 and the photo starts at row 5, with the county label alone in row 4. Either pull the photo up to begin at row 4 and drop the county label onto row 11 beside the lead, or restate the idea so it matches the layout.",
      "Row 4 holds only a 1-line label spanning columns 1–6, leaving a near-empty band between headline and photo. Move the county label up to sit tight under the headline at the bottom of row 3, and let the photo start at row 4. It can then span rows 4–10 at 7 rows tall.",
      "The nearby list sits in rows 6–7, but its two entries occupy only the top half of row 6. That leaves a dead gap between the label in row 5 and the list. Put the list directly under the label at the top of row 6, and give row 7 to the map so the pinfield spans rows 7–10.",
      "In the list, 'Ian Curtis Memorial Stone' and 'Jodrell Bank Observatory' wrap to two lines in a 4-column measure. That breaks the row rhythm with the right-aligned km figures. Either set the names one size smaller so each fits on one line within columns 9–11, with distances in column 12, or let each entry occupy a full baseline pair consistently.",
      "The map pinfield drifts in the middle of columns 9–12 with no frame and no marked town centre. The 1.21 km relationship that the idea rests on is not legible. Anchor the pinfield to the column 9 left edge and the row 10 bottom edge, and label the town pin and the stone pin with their list numbers 01/02.",
      "The lead in columns 1–8, rows 11–12, is set large and competes with the photo. Its last line nearly touches the footer rule. Reduce it one step so it fits in row 11 plus half of row 12, and align its first baseline with the first baseline of the distances text in columns 9–12, which currently sits higher.",
      "The distances text in columns 9–12 is grey on near-black and reads as an afterthought. Raise it to the same off-white as the list, or tie it to the map by placing it directly under the pinfield's bottom edge in row 10.",
      "The photo's small white rule along its bottom edge and the '1' index box in the bottom-left corner add noise inside the 8-column span. Remove the rule so the photo edge aligns cleanly with the row 10 bottom line.",
      "Color is monochrome off-white on black with no accent. Introduce one accent, for example on the stone pin in the map and the '01' index in the list. That would carry the idea's link between the photo and the pin."
    ],
    "summary": "Clean, rigorous, but the stated idea isn't delivered: the headline doesn't sit over the photo, and the map doesn't show the 1.21 km relationship. Tighten rows 4–7, anchor the pinfield, and use one accent to link the stone, the list and the pin.",
    "mean": 5.8
